s that commit 58d8d91ec1 may have broken something with stderr collection, but I'm not familiar enough with the rplugin support to determine for sure what's going on.\r\n\r\nUsing the deoplete rplugin, I ran into some issues with a not-before-seen E725 \"Calling dict function without Dictionary: provider#stderr_collector\" error, which I reported as Shougo/deoplete.nvim#520 but it seems to actually be a neovim issue.\r\n\r\nCommit 58d8d91ec1 introduced a dictionary function `provider#stderr_collector(chan_id, data, event)` which seems to be called incorrectly by the refactored code, at least in this case. I'm not able to obtain anything useful from the runtime log, is there any way to get a traceback on viml errors? \r\n\r\nIn the `-V9` runtime log, the error comes seemingly out of the blue:\r\n\r\n```\r\n chdir(/Users/mqudsi/Projects/messagebridge)                                 \r\n chdir(src)                                                                  \r\n chdir(/Users/mqudsi/Projects/messagebridge)                                 \r\n chdir(/Users/mqudsi/Projects/messagebridge)                                 \r\n chdir(src)                                                                  \r\n chdir(/Users/mqudsi/Projects/messagebridge)                                 \r\n E725: Calling dict function without Dictionary: provider#stderr_collector\r\n E725: Calling dict function without Dictionary: provider#stderr_collector   \r\n Executing InsertLeave Auto commands for \"*\"\r\n autocommand setlocal hlsearch lz                                            \r\n\r\n Executing InsertLeave Auto commands for \"*\"                                 \r\n autocommand call s:on_insert_leave()\r\n                                                                             \r\n autocommand call s:timer_end()\r\n```\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"jamessan","id":112971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjk3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112971?v=4","gravat